# loombox local dev loop env (copy to .env.dev.local, chmod 600, never commit).
# scripts/dev.sh creates .env.dev.local from this file automatically on its
# first run and tells you exactly what to fill in - you shouldn't normally
# need to copy this by hand. Loaded via `set -a; source .env.dev.local`.
#
# This is NOT shaped like deploy/relay/.env.example or
# deploy/node/loombox-node.env.example: those configure a real deployment
# against real infra end to end. This only needs the handful of values that
# are genuinely per-operator (an OAuth app you register yourself, credentials
# only you can mint). Everything else the loop needs - ports, DATABASE_URL,
# LOOMBOX_TRUSTED_ORIGINS, and so on - is a fixed, zero-config literal
# scripts/dev.sh sets itself; see that script if you need to change one.

# --- GitHub OAuth (required) ------------------------------------------------
#
# The relay's real Better Auth GitHub login, exactly as prodbox runs it - no
# dev stub, per SPEC. One-time setup, about two minutes:
#
#   1. https://github.com/settings/developers -> OAuth Apps -> New OAuth App
#      (equivalently: Settings > Developer settings > OAuth Apps > New OAuth App)
#   2. Homepage URL:               http://localhost:5173
#   3. Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:8790/api/auth/callback/github
#   4. Register the app, then "Generate a new client secret" and copy both
#      values below.
#
# Why localhost and not this devbox's tailnet IP: http://localhost is a
# secure context, so window.crypto.subtle exists with no TLS certificate and
# no browser flags - the E2E crypto (AMK generation/unwrap, SPEC §8) needs
# it, the same reason AGENTS.md's desktop-debugging notes give for the
# Electron app. It also means the callback URL registered with GitHub never
# breaks when this devbox's tailnet IP changes, unlike a tailnet-IP callback
# would.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Better Auth signing secret (auto-filled) -------------------------------
#
# scripts/dev.sh generates this into your .env.dev.local (openssl rand
# -base64 32) the first time it finds this empty, then writes it back to the
# file so later runs reuse the same value. Leave it blank; there's no reason
# to set it by hand, and rotating it just invalidates dev login sessions
# (harmless - sign in again).
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# --- node daemon (optional at first run) ------------------------------------
#
# Both blank at first: scripts/dev.sh starts relay + web and SKIPS the node,
# printing this same one-time flow. See deploy/node/loombox-node.env.example
# for what each field means in full - this just documents how to obtain them
# for THIS loop specifically:
#
#   1. Bring the loop up (scripts/dev.sh) and sign in at
#      http://localhost:5173 with the GitHub account you'll develop as.
#   2. In the app: Settings > Recovery Code -> set one up. Paste it below as
#      LOOMBOX_RECOVERY_CODE.
#   3. Re-run scripts/dev.sh. LOOMBOX_AUTH_TOKEN is still blank, so it prints
#      the exact one-off command to run the node by hand; that command
#      prints a short code and names where to approve it
#      (http://localhost:5173/device). Approve it there, in the same
#      signed-in browser, and the node prints back a device token.
#   4. Paste that token below as LOOMBOX_AUTH_TOKEN and re-run scripts/dev.sh
#      once more - the node now starts automatically, no browser step,
#      exactly like a real device would.
LOOMBOX_AUTH_TOKEN=
LOOMBOX_RECOVERY_CODE=
